WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.860
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.130 --> 00:07.070
Can I court you, Time?

3
00:10.670 --> 00:13.000
But I'll forget everything before

4
00:13.000 --> 00:15.400
and get to know you all over again.

5
00:15.400 --> 00:17.070
This is the last time.

6
00:17.070 --> 00:18.100
Do it right.

7
00:18.100 --> 00:19.470
I don't want to hurt again.

8
00:19.470 --> 00:21.600
Do you know everywhere I looked for you?

9
00:21.600 --> 00:23.170
You weren't fucking anywhere.

10
00:23.170 --> 00:26.130
I'm starting to fear my love will hurt you again.

11
00:26.700 --> 00:28.430
I love you, too.

12
00:28.870 --> 00:30.570
It's me! / Hey!

13
00:30.570 --> 00:31.630
Your snack guy.

14
00:31.630 --> 00:32.770
I don't like this!

15
00:33.130 --> 00:34.100
You psycho!

16
00:34.100 --> 00:36.730
Then why'd you cheat on me with him?

17
00:36.730 --> 00:40.430
But it doesn't matter anymore, because today you're mine.

18
00:40.900 --> 00:42.530
What the fuck, you bastard?

19
00:42.870 --> 00:43.870
Star.

20
00:43.870 --> 00:45.400
Din...

21
00:46.830 --> 00:49.000
I'm sorry I'm late.

22
00:49.370 --> 00:51.330
Thanks for helping Star, man.

23
00:51.330 --> 00:52.470
He's my brother too.

24
00:52.470 --> 00:54.600
All I thought was, I can't die yet.

25
00:54.870 --> 00:56.630
I still want to wake up to you.

26
00:56.630 --> 00:57.700
Small as you are,

27
00:57.700 --> 00:59.700
how are you this strong?

28
00:59.700 --> 01:02.100
I promise I'll take good care of you.

29
01:02.600 --> 01:04.500
I'll get in through the quota round.

30
01:04.500 --> 01:07.400
Fine. But I have one more condition.

31
01:07.400 --> 01:09.570
If you don't get in this round,

32
01:09.570 --> 01:11.800
you'll go to the university I choose

33
01:11.800 --> 01:13.170
and the faculty I pick.

34
01:13.170 --> 01:14.900
Do you understand me, Din?

35
01:18.270 --> 01:22.330
"Not selected"

36
01:24.330 --> 01:25.730
Not applying for med?

37
01:25.730 --> 01:27.000
Let me have this, Mom.

38
01:27.530 --> 01:29.470
You really want to study here?

39
01:29.470 --> 01:32.630
If you want to decide, you have to deliver.

40
01:43.600 --> 01:46.870
"Time, tell Star for me that I didn't get in this round."

41
01:46.870 --> 01:50.600
"But don't overthink it. I'll get in through the quota round."

42
01:50.600 --> 01:53.030
"I'll be busier, but I won't disappear."

43
01:53.030 --> 01:55.430
"Please understand."

44
02:05.030 --> 02:08.130
"Star's read it. He asked me to send you this picture."

45
02:08.600 --> 02:11.330
Your future matters to me.

46
02:11.330 --> 02:13.430
Give it your all.

47
02:13.430 --> 02:16.870
I'll take good care of myself, for you too.

48
04:39.200 --> 04:40.600
Confess.

49
04:43.530 --> 04:45.670
Shit, how did I never figure that out?

50
04:46.470 --> 04:48.600
This is fucking news to me.

51
04:49.500 --> 04:51.230
Not just you.

52
04:51.230 --> 04:54.130
I always thought he liked Tonnam.

53
04:54.900 --> 04:55.900
What about him?

54
04:56.230 --> 04:58.370
Does he like you?

55
05:07.300 --> 05:09.670
Well, if I'm not just kidding myself,

56
05:10.230 --> 05:12.470
I don't think he finds me annoying.

57
05:12.470 --> 05:14.430
He just needs some time to think.

58
05:15.730 --> 05:17.800
I've been watching Time for a year now.

59
05:17.800 --> 05:20.600
I know what he likes and doesn't like,

60
05:20.600 --> 05:22.530
what makes him happy.

61
05:23.370 --> 05:26.300
I love how well he takes care of himself.

62
05:27.400 --> 05:30.070
I just want to take care of him even better.

63
05:31.900 --> 05:35.130
With this one, I'm dead serious.

64
05:47.770 --> 05:49.500
I know you can do it, man.

65
05:50.030 --> 05:54.030
The thing is, how much is Time going to open up to you?

66
05:56.500 --> 05:58.230
No idea.

67
05:58.230 --> 06:00.170
But I don't want to pressure him.

68
06:01.870 --> 06:03.470
Same as you, right?

69
06:03.470 --> 06:06.200
For me, I've already told him how I feel.

70
06:06.630 --> 06:08.200
If he hasn't shut the door,

71
06:08.200 --> 06:09.730
I still have hope.

72
06:09.730 --> 06:11.570
At least Time seems smart.

73
06:11.570 --> 06:12.770
Unlike Fuen.

74
06:13.230 --> 06:14.230
A year of hints,

75
06:14.230 --> 06:15.330
and still nothing.

76
06:15.330 --> 06:17.330
Sure, Mr. Perfect.

77
06:17.330 --> 06:19.330
Like you've never screwed up.

78
06:19.330 --> 06:21.630
A one-man show and a hat-trick,

79
06:21.630 --> 06:24.070
plus two more for five goals, right?

80
06:24.830 --> 06:25.970
Ow!

81
06:26.870 --> 06:28.970
But I seriously respect you, Physics,

82
06:29.700 --> 06:31.900
for never giving up on Fuen.

83
06:35.900 --> 06:37.030
What can I do?

84
06:37.870 --> 06:39.600
I already fell for him.

85
06:43.570 --> 06:45.670
But you and Time,

86
06:45.670 --> 06:48.900
give it long enough and it'll be the same for you.

87
06:52.000 --> 06:53.600
Are you going to give up first?

88
06:54.870 --> 06:55.870
I don't think so.

89
06:57.670 --> 06:59.830
Unless he tells me to stop.

90
07:03.770 --> 07:06.800
Students, get ready to present. Stop playing now.

91
07:18.300 --> 07:20.270
Hey, play it right this time, okay?

92
07:20.270 --> 07:22.230
Give it your all. I'm recording.

93
07:23.270 --> 07:26.570
Hey, wait. When the clip opens,

94
07:26.570 --> 07:29.400
backs turned first, then turn when the music hits?

95
07:29.400 --> 07:34.000
When we perform for real, if we put a lot of feeling into it, it'll be amazing.

96
07:34.000 --> 07:36.600
Hey, Art. That solo part,

97
07:36.600 --> 07:38.800
make it more hype. It'll be fun.

98
07:38.800 --> 07:39.570
Got it.

99
07:39.570 --> 07:40.570
Let's go!

100
07:41.500 --> 07:44.430
3, 2, 1.

101
08:05.670 --> 08:11.100
♪ Have you ever felt it — no matter how far the days carry us ♪

102
08:11.100 --> 08:15.370
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on the story of that day ♪

103
08:15.370 --> 08:22.200
♪ it warms my heart all over again ♪

104
08:22.700 --> 08:28.330
♪ Looking at the photos some nights before I sleep, I smile to myself ♪

105
08:28.330 --> 08:32.630
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on you and me ♪

106
08:32.630 --> 08:37.770
♪ a time I've never once forgotten ♪

107
08:40.330 --> 08:47.570
♪ However long the years run on, my heart still won't forget ♪

108
08:48.900 --> 08:56.200
♪ Even if we had to part in the end, that time is still just as it was ♪

109
08:56.200 --> 09:00.300
♪ It's all still so clear inside me ♪

110
09:00.300 --> 09:04.370
♪ I still remember all our good times, just the same ♪

111
09:04.370 --> 09:08.670
♪ The days we smiled at each other, the days we were close ♪

112
09:08.670 --> 09:13.430
♪ None of it has ever gone away ♪

113
09:13.430 --> 09:17.530
♪ It's all still so clear, it never faded ♪

114
09:17.530 --> 09:21.770
♪ Even if today we have to go our separate ways ♪

115
09:21.770 --> 09:26.170
♪ However far apart you and I may be ♪

116
09:26.170 --> 09:30.070
♪ our time together is still here in my heart ♪

117
09:30.600 --> 09:34.370
♪ It's all still so clear ♪

118
09:35.970 --> 09:42.330
♪ I'm only just learning what it's like without you ♪

119
09:42.330 --> 09:46.230
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on you and me ♪

120
09:46.230 --> 09:53.070
♪ those days make me miss you, my dear ♪

121
10:08.800 --> 10:09.800
Woo!

122
10:33.630 --> 10:34.870
Tired?

123
10:38.200 --> 10:43.130
Yeah... but I want to finish this page first.

124
10:51.630 --> 10:53.430
If we go to England,

125
10:53.800 --> 10:55.070
what do you want to do?

126
11:03.370 --> 11:04.870
Ride the bus.

127
11:09.400 --> 11:10.570
Isn't that a train?

128
11:12.500 --> 11:13.500
I don't know.

129
11:13.500 --> 11:15.200
I've never been.

130
11:19.470 --> 11:22.600
But I want to see how people live there.

131
11:24.700 --> 11:27.230
What else?

132
11:31.730 --> 11:39.430
Walk around town and take photos. But you're taking mine.

133
11:42.830 --> 11:50.300
And a market tour. But promise me

134
11:50.930 --> 11:53.500
you'll help me save. Don't eat too much.

135
11:56.570 --> 11:57.730
Deal.

136
12:00.300 --> 12:03.670
Is there anywhere you especially want to go?

137
12:12.330 --> 12:13.330
A church.

138
12:17.270 --> 12:19.530
I want to go to a church with you.

139
12:27.700 --> 12:32.400
Hmm. But what you just said,

140
12:32.400 --> 12:36.000
I... don't get what you mean.

141
12:39.000 --> 12:41.970
But wherever you go, I'm ready to go too.

142
12:45.300 --> 12:47.800
I mean everywhere you just mentioned.

143
12:48.700 --> 12:50.500
I'll go with you.

144
13:05.230 --> 13:07.770
So, is it the train or the bus?

145
13:07.800 --> 13:09.430
You'll find out.

146
13:09.430 --> 13:11.200
Let me pass the interview first.

147
13:37.900 --> 13:41.500
Guys, should we send the clip now?

148
13:41.500 --> 13:47.230
Send it. They say today's an auspicious day, perfect for competing.

149
13:47.530 --> 13:48.930
Based on whose horoscope?

150
13:48.930 --> 13:49.930
Thanop's.

151
13:49.930 --> 13:52.630
Huh? Why not check your own?

152
13:52.630 --> 13:55.600
Oh, I did. I'm doomed.

153
13:56.600 --> 13:58.800
What about Jet's and Art's?

154
13:58.800 --> 14:00.870
Ugh, even worse than mine.

155
14:00.870 --> 14:01.770
Seriously?

156
14:01.770 --> 14:03.530
Where are those two now?

157
14:03.530 --> 14:05.570
They probably rushed off to tutoring.

158
14:05.930 --> 14:08.370
So whose luck do we use to enter the contest?

159
14:08.370 --> 14:09.370
Good point.

160
14:12.070 --> 14:14.070
Mine's not bad.

161
14:14.400 --> 14:17.800
But I should watch out for breaking things.

162
14:18.470 --> 14:20.730
But entering can't break anything.

163
14:20.730 --> 14:21.770
Yeah, easy.

164
14:21.770 --> 14:22.800
Here we go!

165
14:23.230 --> 14:26.270
Let's do this!

166
14:51.030 --> 14:53.930
There you are. I've been looking all over for you.

167
14:55.430 --> 14:57.330
When will you stop using

168
14:57.330 --> 14:59.300
council perks to study here so late?

169
15:00.930 --> 15:02.700
Studying at home is way better.

170
15:03.130 --> 15:07.330
Hmm, I think it's chill here. More comfortable.

171
15:07.330 --> 15:11.200
The school closes at seven. Going home late is dangerous.

172
15:12.700 --> 15:14.300
I'll think about it.

173
15:15.030 --> 15:17.130
But I still don't like studying at home.

174
15:17.830 --> 15:20.700
Or do you have a place you'd recommend?

175
15:25.500 --> 15:26.770
Your friend's place?

176
15:28.470 --> 15:30.670
My friends are all taken.

177
15:33.100 --> 15:36.730
Then, from now on, whenever you study at school,

178
15:36.730 --> 15:38.130
I'll come keep you company.

179
15:42.730 --> 15:43.830
Thank you.

180
15:44.800 --> 15:45.800
Hungry?

181
15:46.130 --> 15:47.770
I'll get you something to eat.

182
15:48.730 --> 15:50.030
Whoa, Time!

183
15:54.030 --> 15:55.600
Before looking after others,

184
15:56.770 --> 15:58.970
stop being so clumsy first.

185
16:05.730 --> 16:07.500
Come on, I'm hungry.

186
16:38.930 --> 16:40.570
I'd better head home.

187
16:42.070 --> 16:43.530
See you, see you.

188
16:43.530 --> 16:45.570
Get home safe. Bye-bye.

189
16:45.570 --> 16:47.000
Bye.

190
16:50.270 --> 16:51.670
Yeah, see you.

191
16:52.300 --> 16:53.770
Get home safe.

192
16:55.900 --> 17:01.530
Why didn't you tell me you were coming? What if I'd left already?

193
17:02.130 --> 17:04.000
Then I guess I'd get surprised back.

194
17:04.599 --> 17:06.000
That's not okay, Aof.

195
17:06.270 --> 17:09.369
Next time, you tell me before you come. Got it?

196
17:10.069 --> 17:12.970
Yes... I get it.

197
17:15.569 --> 17:18.099
Next time, I'll tell you first.

198
17:19.000 --> 17:20.000
Good boy.

199
17:20.000 --> 17:22.030
So how was practice today? Tired?

200
17:26.000 --> 17:28.069
Ugh, ugh, ugh.

201
17:31.530 --> 17:34.270
I'm so tired.

202
17:38.070 --> 17:42.370
But we sent the clip just in time.

203
17:45.270 --> 17:46.470
Whoa.

204
17:47.500 --> 17:50.370
I should've gone up and listened outside.

205
17:50.370 --> 17:52.500
I missed hearing you sing again.

206
17:53.730 --> 17:54.730
Then...

207
17:55.730 --> 17:57.230
Want me to sing for you?

208
17:58.230 --> 17:59.230
Really?

209
18:00.000 --> 18:01.170
Yeah, really.

210
18:02.670 --> 18:04.330
Okay, pick a song.

211
18:05.100 --> 18:07.100
If it's your voice,

212
18:07.100 --> 18:08.700
any song is fine.

213
18:13.230 --> 18:14.630
Then...

214
18:16.470 --> 18:17.870
Hold on.

215
18:33.030 --> 18:36.400
This one, then.

216
18:41.670 --> 18:49.470
♪ ...you gave me, that day we sat side by side ♪

217
18:51.000 --> 18:59.030
♪ We once made a promise that we'd have each other ♪

218
19:01.530 --> 19:11.200
♪ That day everything seemed so clear, we laughed all day ♪

219
19:12.770 --> 19:17.530
♪ that I still remember now ♪

220
19:24.100 --> 19:30.900
♪ Because this heart of mine is still waiting, only for you ♪

221
19:40.670 --> 19:42.570
I wrote this song myself.

222
19:44.870 --> 19:46.970
It's not finished yet,

223
19:48.700 --> 19:50.700
but I wanted you to hear it first.

224
19:52.600 --> 19:53.800
Thank you.

225
19:55.430 --> 19:59.600
I don't know why, but... all of a sudden...

226
20:00.130 --> 20:02.270
the tears just started coming.

227
20:04.070 --> 20:05.730
There, there.

228
20:07.400 --> 20:08.900
Such a crybaby.

229
20:13.500 --> 20:17.470
I'll finish this song and make it complete.

230
20:18.500 --> 20:20.000
And when that day comes,

231
20:20.000 --> 20:22.600
don't forget to let me hear it first.

232
20:23.300 --> 20:24.300
I won't forget.

233
20:24.800 --> 20:26.270
Promise.

234
20:31.000 --> 20:32.670
Thank you, Chemi.

235
20:38.300 --> 20:40.500
Can you play it for me one more time?

236
20:43.600 --> 20:45.230
You're welcome.

237
20:47.400 --> 20:48.500
Let me lean on you.

238
21:41.330 --> 21:43.700
You have tutoring at school today, right?

239
21:44.800 --> 21:48.470
I'll drop you off. I have errands around there anyway.

240
21:50.370 --> 21:51.470
Okay, Mom.

241
21:51.970 --> 21:54.870
When do you finish? I'll pick you up if I can.

242
21:54.870 --> 21:58.600
Probably evening, Mom. I'm meeting Chok and Tonnam to keep studying.

243
21:58.600 --> 22:01.270
I see. Will you be home for dinner?

244
22:01.270 --> 22:02.830
Don't wait for me, Mom.

245
22:02.830 --> 22:05.400
I'll probably eat before I come home.

246
22:05.400 --> 22:07.430
Let me eat quickly, then I'll take you.

247
22:07.430 --> 22:08.230
Okay, Mom.

248
22:08.230 --> 22:08.870
Okay.

249
22:09.930 --> 22:11.470
Attention, all M.6 students.

250
22:11.470 --> 22:15.730
After school today, the guidance counselor will be giving university advice.

251
22:20.000 --> 22:21.170
Hey, Time.

252
22:21.600 --> 22:23.300
You've been getting home late

253
22:23.300 --> 22:25.770
because you stay up with Tang while he studies?

254
22:26.330 --> 22:28.800
Yeah. You're never free when we ask anymore,

255
22:28.800 --> 22:30.470
but you're with Tang everywhere.

256
22:31.000 --> 22:32.570
So, in conclusion,

257
22:32.570 --> 22:34.500
you like Tang, right?

258
22:38.630 --> 22:40.400
Anything to say in your defense?

259
22:40.400 --> 22:42.130
Otherwise, the court rules that...

260
22:42.870 --> 22:44.770
you like him.

261
22:46.630 --> 22:47.630
I confess.

262
22:47.630 --> 22:48.970
Lock me up.

263
22:48.970 --> 22:50.770
The defendant turns himself in.

264
22:51.200 --> 22:53.200
But give me a little more time to think.

265
22:54.070 --> 22:56.230
Time, where are you going to get more time?

266
22:56.230 --> 22:58.300
Tang's about to graduate, you know.

267
22:58.300 --> 22:59.600
Yeah.

268
23:00.200 --> 23:03.370
So let him graduate. Then I'll know if he changes his mind.

269
23:03.370 --> 23:04.900
You can play hard to get,

270
23:04.900 --> 23:06.500
but if he gives up,

271
23:06.500 --> 23:08.700
you'll be the one moping.

272
23:09.200 --> 23:11.970
Yeah. Good guys don't come along that often these days.

273
23:11.970 --> 23:15.170
Let Tang slip away, and who knows if you'll find another.

274
23:15.170 --> 23:19.000
Honestly, Time, we're rooting for Tang.

275
23:19.000 --> 23:20.670
Ever since you met him,

276
23:20.670 --> 23:23.530
you've looked so happy, you know?

277
23:24.300 --> 23:25.830
I know.

278
23:26.330 --> 23:28.570
I know myself. When I'm with Tang,

279
23:28.570 --> 23:30.270
I'm so damn happy.

280
23:30.930 --> 23:34.570
But I want to stay with this feeling a little longer.

281
23:36.030 --> 23:38.500
I'm just not sure

282
23:38.500 --> 23:39.930
if what I'm feeling

283
23:39.930 --> 23:42.530
is because I really like him, or...

284
23:43.000 --> 23:45.030
just because he's being nice to me.

285
23:46.900 --> 23:50.100
Damn, that's deep.

286
23:55.270 --> 23:57.200
I know you look after yourself,

287
23:57.200 --> 24:00.500
but let me care for you better.

288
24:06.270 --> 24:08.370
I like him!

289
24:08.370 --> 24:10.600
Yeah, we know.

290
24:21.130 --> 24:22.730
How was today?

291
24:23.730 --> 24:24.730
Chill.

292
24:24.730 --> 24:26.370
I could take the exam tomorrow.

293
24:26.670 --> 24:28.070
Good to be confident.

294
24:28.070 --> 24:29.470
Want to see a movie?

295
24:29.470 --> 24:30.370
Got tickets.

296
24:30.370 --> 24:31.200
Sure.

297
24:32.030 --> 24:33.400
Ooh, look at you two.

298
24:33.400 --> 24:35.030
Where are you off to?

299
24:35.030 --> 24:36.030
Butt out.

300
24:36.500 --> 24:37.830
Just kidding.

301
24:37.830 --> 24:38.830
Okay.

302
24:39.770 --> 24:41.100
What about you guys?

303
24:41.100 --> 24:42.170
Going to a movie.

304
24:42.170 --> 24:44.270
Hey, we're going to see a movie too.

305
24:45.030 --> 24:46.070
Which one?

306
24:49.400 --> 24:50.400
This one.

307
24:50.400 --> 24:51.400
Hey!

308
24:51.800 --> 24:52.970
Same movie.

309
24:52.970 --> 24:55.130
Oh, great. Let's go.

310
24:55.130 --> 24:57.100
Let's go, come on.

311
25:09.570 --> 25:11.130
This one looks good too.

312
25:12.270 --> 25:14.530
This one's better. It's trending right now.

313
25:14.530 --> 25:16.730
Four seats, please.

314
25:17.170 --> 25:19.470
Yeah, I want to see the same one as Time.

315
25:19.470 --> 25:21.000
Yeah, this one's fine.

316
25:25.000 --> 25:26.600
Oh, Star.

317
25:26.930 --> 25:28.270
Oh, Din.

318
25:28.270 --> 25:29.830
You're here for a movie too?

319
25:29.830 --> 25:30.930
Yes.

320
25:31.830 --> 25:33.530
Same movie as us?

321
25:34.030 --> 25:36.900
Of course. I already booked online.

322
25:39.870 --> 25:42.000
I booked. He didn't.

323
25:42.000 --> 25:43.730
Same thing.

324
25:48.130 --> 25:51.630
Nice. We didn't come together, but we're watching together.

325
25:51.630 --> 25:53.470
It's totally fate.

326
25:56.900 --> 25:59.770
Okay, come on. Let's go!

327
27:05.730 --> 27:10.230
Trust me, this place is really good. It's famous around here.

328
27:10.230 --> 27:11.830
Star, what do you want?

329
27:11.830 --> 27:13.200
Whatever you like.

330
27:13.200 --> 27:15.730
Their desserts are amazing here.

331
27:15.730 --> 27:17.670
What do you like to eat?

332
27:17.670 --> 27:19.070
I like...

333
27:42.030 --> 27:44.770
Your mom doesn't know about Star at all?

334
27:46.030 --> 27:47.830
I never told her.

335
27:49.400 --> 27:51.700
I've never seen Aunt Om like this.

336
27:52.330 --> 27:54.530
It's going to be okay, right, Din?

337
27:54.970 --> 27:57.030
That's so scary.

338
27:58.100 --> 27:59.700
I don't know.

339
28:21.700 --> 28:27.170
Din, I think everything your mom said is right.

340
28:28.070 --> 28:29.600
What matters most for you now

341
28:29.600 --> 28:32.300
is focusing on university.

342
28:38.200 --> 28:40.430
I think we should take some space,

343
28:40.430 --> 28:42.300
until you get into a school.

344
28:45.030 --> 28:47.570
Wait, I already told you...

345
28:47.570 --> 28:49.570
Din, we're going home.

346
28:50.330 --> 28:53.300
No, Mom. We already talked about this.

347
28:53.830 --> 28:55.430
Why are you doing this?

348
28:55.700 --> 28:56.930
What did you tell Star?

349
28:56.930 --> 28:59.230
Your mom didn't say anything bad.

350
28:59.670 --> 29:01.600
This was all my idea.

351
29:03.070 --> 29:04.530
You know what?

352
29:05.070 --> 29:09.130
Your future means a lot to me.

353
29:09.130 --> 29:12.930
And if... being in your life makes it worse,

354
29:13.530 --> 29:14.900
I don't want to be in it.

355
29:14.900 --> 29:18.430
Star, you don't make my life worse.

356
29:19.470 --> 29:21.270
Can't I make one mistake, Mom?

357
29:21.430 --> 29:22.430
I messed up.

358
29:22.970 --> 29:24.030
I know.

359
29:25.530 --> 29:27.900
But I'm trying to make it work.

360
29:28.470 --> 29:30.830
Din, I've always listened to you.

361
29:30.830 --> 29:33.770
Whenever you said you'd do something, you did it.

362
29:34.030 --> 29:37.130
But this time, I just want to know if you failed

363
29:37.770 --> 29:39.770
because you can't balance your love life

364
29:39.770 --> 29:41.870
with your own life.

365
29:45.600 --> 29:47.700
Then you have to prove

366
29:47.700 --> 29:49.800
that your mom is wrong.

367
29:51.100 --> 29:54.900
Because in the end, I don't want us to end like this either.

368
30:03.600 --> 30:04.830
Yes, Mom.

369
30:05.430 --> 30:06.630
I understand.

370
30:07.270 --> 30:09.070
And I'll prove it to you.

371
30:15.100 --> 30:18.600
Star, trust me.

372
30:27.800 --> 30:28.870
Star.

373
30:30.430 --> 30:32.170
I want to ask you something.

374
30:35.030 --> 30:36.730
What is it?

375
30:42.470 --> 30:44.230
If we have to be apart...

376
30:44.230 --> 30:47.230
could you post stories so I can see

377
30:47.230 --> 30:51.330
what you're up to? So I won't worry.

378
30:59.100 --> 31:00.800
Thank you.

379
31:38.630 --> 31:40.430
How was your day, Aof?

380
31:41.200 --> 31:43.230
I'd rather hear about yours.

381
31:43.430 --> 31:44.430
So today, right,

382
31:44.430 --> 31:47.630
Thanop and I went out for shabu.

383
31:47.630 --> 31:51.030
Then I told Thanop to check if the pot was hot yet.

384
31:51.030 --> 31:54.270
He grabbed the pot and blistered his hand like this.

385
31:54.270 --> 31:55.530
I was so confused.

386
31:55.530 --> 31:58.370
Instead of the pork, he put his own hand on it.

387
31:58.370 --> 31:59.370
He screamed!

388
31:59.370 --> 32:00.730
Like a monkey, Chemi.

389
32:00.730 --> 32:03.170
Then he ran off and jumped into the canal.

390
32:03.570 --> 32:05.670
It was so damn funny. I even filmed it.

391
32:05.670 --> 32:08.030
I'll show you the clip when we see each other.

392
32:19.000 --> 32:20.000
Chemi?

393
32:21.570 --> 32:22.570
Chemi?

394
32:24.870 --> 32:26.200
Did you fall asleep?

395
32:28.530 --> 32:29.530
Chemi?

396
32:33.330 --> 32:35.070
Sweet dreams, Chemi.

397
33:09.130 --> 33:10.130
Din.

398
33:10.730 --> 33:12.400
Don't overdo it, sweetie.

399
33:19.500 --> 33:21.000
Mom.

400
33:23.370 --> 33:24.870
I'm not mad at you, Mom.

401
33:28.500 --> 33:31.100
But I want you to give Star a chance.

402
33:33.100 --> 33:34.530
It doesn't have to be now.

403
33:35.300 --> 33:36.900
Just let me get in first.

404
33:39.030 --> 33:40.900
Study hard, sweetie.

405
34:29.800 --> 34:31.130
Want some water, man?

406
34:32.070 --> 34:33.530
Let's get to the point.

407
34:39.300 --> 34:40.300
How are you doing?

408
34:43.270 --> 34:44.670
I'm okay.

409
34:45.770 --> 34:47.469
Hey.

410
34:48.429 --> 34:49.969
Did you fight with your mom?

411
34:50.400 --> 34:51.800
Did she lay a hand on you?

412
34:52.400 --> 34:53.929
Are you hurt anywhere?

413
34:54.800 --> 34:56.270
I'm worried about you, man.

414
34:59.330 --> 35:00.870
Why would we fight?

415
35:00.870 --> 35:02.370
We already talked it out.

416
35:03.500 --> 35:05.400
I'm really fine.

417
35:06.430 --> 35:08.500
Once the exam's over, it'll all be over.

418
35:12.100 --> 35:13.700
So since that day,

419
35:13.700 --> 35:15.770
you haven't talked to your little star?

420
35:19.900 --> 35:21.170
Little star?

421
35:22.270 --> 35:23.470
Din's little star.

422
35:23.470 --> 35:25.500
Not Patrick Star, okay?

423
35:28.370 --> 35:29.830
Are we done here?

424
35:29.830 --> 35:32.170
Then let me study for my future.

425
35:33.400 --> 35:34.900
Then we've got futures too.

426
35:34.900 --> 35:36.130
We'll study with you.

427
36:47.270 --> 36:49.500
"FUN VIBE / Thapfah Wittayanusorn School"

428
36:57.300 --> 36:58.570
Round two.

429
37:00.300 --> 37:04.100
Each band has to perform three songs.

430
37:04.400 --> 37:07.470
One of them has to be an original.

431
37:09.870 --> 37:11.300
Who's going to write it?

432
37:11.300 --> 37:12.700
Who's writing?

433
37:14.330 --> 37:17.170
Actually, I have a song I've written.

434
37:17.170 --> 37:18.730
It might not be good yet.

435
37:21.030 --> 37:23.230
Let me hear it.

436
37:23.230 --> 37:24.970
Please, can we hear it?

437
38:13.900 --> 38:15.500
Physics. / Hmm?

438
38:15.500 --> 38:17.400
Is this one good enough?

439
38:17.400 --> 38:19.630
It's good. Put it in the portfolio.

440
38:26.300 --> 38:28.800
What about this sketch?

441
38:29.200 --> 38:30.200
Physics.

442
38:31.600 --> 38:34.330
That's great. Go for it, keep it.

443
38:34.930 --> 38:36.970
Okay. / Let's go, let's go!

444
38:53.230 --> 38:55.830
Okay, got it.

445
39:03.930 --> 39:05.830
Every piece is so beautiful.

446
39:06.130 --> 39:07.500
With skills like this,

447
39:08.100 --> 39:09.830
just wait. You'll pass for sure.

448
39:10.400 --> 39:11.970
Is it really good?

449
39:12.900 --> 39:13.900
Of course.

450
39:14.330 --> 39:16.030
Anyone who sees it will say so.

451
39:20.730 --> 39:21.970
What's wrong?

452
39:23.330 --> 39:26.030
Smile. Come on, smile.

453
39:28.900 --> 39:35.770
Be confident. Believe in yourself. Okay? It'll be fine either way.

454
39:35.770 --> 39:40.830
♪ When you turn to me, I can't hold your gaze for long ♪

455
39:40.830 --> 39:46.470
♪ I carry it into my dreams each night, but I can't do a thing about it ♪

456
39:46.470 --> 39:51.730
♪ Every look you send my way makes my heart shake even more ♪

457
39:51.730 --> 39:56.000
♪ One slip and I'm imagining things ♪

458
39:56.800 --> 40:02.270
♪ I slip and give you my heart, I slip and watch you every day ♪

459
40:02.270 --> 40:07.500
♪ My heart can't take it ♪

460
40:07.500 --> 40:13.030
♪ Beside you every day, but I have to act like I don't care ♪

461
40:13.030 --> 40:18.530
♪ We stay just friends, so I keep it inside ♪

462
40:18.530 --> 40:23.870
♪ I want you to know, but I can't cross that line ♪

463
40:23.870 --> 40:28.570
♪ I know what's between us should stay unsaid ♪

464
41:14.400 --> 41:20.630
"Can you come down for a bit? I'm waiting outside your house."

465
42:01.030 --> 42:02.700
Dad, Mom...

466
42:03.500 --> 42:05.370
I'm heading out. Bye.

467
42:05.370 --> 42:06.570
Bye.

468
42:18.530 --> 42:19.300
Hold this.

469
42:37.370 --> 42:39.070
Very good.

470
42:55.370 --> 42:59.200
Sit tight, okay? Don't let go when I take off.

471
43:00.230 --> 43:01.670
Spread your arms.

472
43:27.330 --> 43:29.500
You're the one who taught me this.

473
43:31.200 --> 43:33.270
Yeah, yeah.

474
43:35.170 --> 43:37.130
Okay, we're leaving.

475
43:37.130 --> 43:38.500
Good luck, sweetie.

476
43:38.500 --> 43:39.970
Bye.

477
43:39.970 --> 43:40.970
Bye, son.

478
43:40.970 --> 43:42.630
Even if you guess, guess right.

479
43:42.630 --> 43:44.470
You got it! / Yes.

480
44:21.630 --> 44:23.270
Here.

481
44:32.030 --> 44:33.670
What's wrong?

482
44:33.670 --> 44:35.700
Nervous?

483
44:52.500 --> 44:55.130
Whatever's going on in your head right now,

484
44:55.130 --> 44:56.830
leave it all behind.

485
44:58.970 --> 45:01.030
Just go in and focus on the exam.

486
45:11.400 --> 45:13.400
I know you can do it.

487
45:21.030 --> 45:22.200
Don't worry.

488
45:34.470 --> 45:36.870
No matter what, I'll be right here by your side.

489
46:14.500 --> 46:15.900
Thinking about Din?

490
46:17.530 --> 46:18.530
Yeah.

491
46:19.730 --> 46:22.330
I still don't know how he's doing.

492
46:26.030 --> 46:28.500
How many exams does he have left?

493
46:30.930 --> 46:32.500
Two, I think.

494
46:34.670 --> 46:36.070
Hold it right there.

495
46:36.600 --> 46:37.830
Star.

496
46:41.670 --> 46:43.100
Sneaking photos again?

497
46:43.430 --> 46:46.270
Perfect timing. I'll send it to Din

498
46:46.270 --> 46:48.370
to cheer him on for his exam.

499
47:01.730 --> 47:04.170
The morning exam is about to begin.

500
47:04.170 --> 47:06.000
Please get ready.

501
47:06.000 --> 47:08.970
The papers will be handed out in ten minutes.

502
47:40.900 --> 47:42.930
Time's up. Everyone, pens down.

503
47:46.570 --> 47:49.970
The afternoon exam starts at 1:30 p.m.

504
47:49.970 --> 47:53.530
Please be on time. Thank you.

505
48:25.830 --> 48:28.330
I want something of yours

506
48:29.030 --> 48:30.770
to keep with me.

507
48:30.770 --> 48:32.570
Can you give me something?

508
49:42.330 --> 49:43.600
Dad!

509
50:02.030 --> 50:05.170
"I won't say my son isn't capable. I know you're the best."

510
50:05.170 --> 50:08.400
"I'm proud, but you're focused on the wrong thing. (Din's mom)"

511
50:08.400 --> 50:10.500
"You know who I am and how I think."

512
50:10.500 --> 50:12.100
"I can't lose you. So..."

513
50:12.100 --> 50:13.770
"stay with me. Promise? (Fuen)"

514
50:13.770 --> 50:14.900
"Promise. (Physics)"

515
50:14.900 --> 50:16.970
"I don't want to hold you back. (Star)"

516
50:16.970 --> 50:19.200
"You keep me going, not back. (Din)"

517
50:19.200 --> 50:21.300
"Show her I make you better. (Star)"

518
50:21.670 --> 50:22.830
Look forward to it.

519
50:22.830 --> 50:23.930
I'll listen closely.

520
50:24.500 --> 50:26.800
You're from Thapfah, right?

521
50:27.300 --> 50:30.470
Yes. / Thapfah Wittayanusorn.

522
50:34.600 --> 50:36.470
Your mom told me everything,

523
50:36.470 --> 50:37.770
about the exam and Star.

524
50:37.770 --> 50:39.000
Was I wrong, Dad?

525
50:39.000 --> 50:41.900
Din, let's go see your mom.

526
50:44.900 --> 50:47.330
You know, right? But you shouldn't have, Star.

527
50:47.800 --> 50:49.630
Why did the university email me?

528
50:49.630 --> 50:51.300
An offer from the university?

529
50:51.300 --> 50:52.600
I'm not ready for this.

530
50:52.600 --> 50:54.030
I can't bear to look.
